Apple's second-generation <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> could gain <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mask-face-id/">Face ID</a>, with prototypes already incorporating the technology beneath the outer display, according to <a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/poweronpodcast"><em>Bloomberg</em>'s Mark Gurman</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iPhone-Duo-Open-large-scaled-feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-1072233" /><br/>
In the latest episode of his <a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/poweronpodcast">"Power On" podcast</a>, Gurman described Apple's work on adding facial authentication technology to its foldable iPhone. The company is said to be testing the hardware for a successor expected next fall, but has not finalized whether the feature will ship.<br/>
<br/>
The current, first-generation &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; relies on a fingerprint sensor embedded in its side button, just like the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a>. Its thin design leaves limited space for the depth-sensing components needed for &zwnj;Face ID&zwnj;.<br/>
<br/>
News of the prototype seems to represent a more concrete development of Gurman's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/14/third-gen-iphone-duo-face-id-telephoto-lens/">earlier prediction</a> about future &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; upgrades. In September, he suggested that smaller components and advances in artificial intelligence could help Apple add &zwnj;Face ID&zwnj; and a dedicated telephoto camera by the third generation.<br/>
<br/>
Gurman also said that Apple is considering adding an Action button to a future &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;. The feature is noticeably lacking on the current model.<br/>
